{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And I will clothe him with your tunic.</b> Every appointed officer has a designated tunic and sash, just as the sages of Athens would gird a designated sash." "<b>And he shall be a father.</b> A teacher who teaches good and loves like a father."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "'אטונס' read as Athens; the identification is standard in medieval Hebrew literature."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:42.387339926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}